        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Clean up wording for Safari AccentColor support]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29456</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29456"/>
        <updated>2026-04-11T16:46:57.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10727862?u=2064158183f11ce7710feb1792c00fe81d4e0250&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">I found the current wording very confusing:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Only supports a fallback: The native color when accent colour (in macOS' appearance panel) is set to 'multicolour'. On iOS falls back to the blue accent colour</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">I'm replacing it with this wording which I hope is more clear and correct:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Always uses the system default accent color, blue. This accidentally produces the correct result when the system accent color is Multicolor.</p>
</blockquote>]]></content>
